From e705d05c715054f05c7026c06f5cf559ce056cc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:44:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): dispatch a waited-on parent first and
 tell its waiting chat when it stays unclaimed

Defect kanban-447c98343f: a rollout card waited 2 h on a p0 parent that sat ready behind 61 older p0 leaves
(lane order was priority then age only) and the waiting chat heard nothing.

- DISPATCH_ORDER (lane_rows, list_tasks default, worker-node candidates, queue position): effective priority =
  max(own, waiting todo children), then cards with a waiting child, then age. Stored priority unchanged.
- kanban_parent_unclaimed: once per wait, a chat-owned todo child whose dependency wait and parent's ready
  entry are both 30+ min old gets a dependency_parent_unclaimed event (gateway wakes, TUI notice) naming the
  parent, its queue place and the moves (bump, re-place, do it here). post_notice is reusable.
- kanban_show adds queue_hint for a card ready and unclaimed 30+ min.
